 "note_en": "被 + (doer) + verb is the classic passive: 周围的楼房在几秒钟内就被震坏了 \"the buildings around were wrecked by the blast within seconds.\" When the doer isn't named, 被 goes straight before the verb, as here. The verb usually carries a result (震坏 \"shake until broken\"), because the Chinese passive tends to report something that happened to the subject, often something bad.",
